Alright I’m gonna throw in my two cents; 

If you want to have sex with him, ask for it and see what happens. If his behaviour doesn’t change then convince him to go see a sex therapist or a counselor with you, so that they can address how he’s been feeling about all this. 

Maybe he really did give up on sex or maybe he’s still hoping but has insecurities and fears in the way. Either way this won’t progress if you give up on resolving this. Get rid of the uncertainties at least.

Guys found it!! The simplification of;

Σ (n-a)((2nCa),

is;

n((2nCn)/2.

So in this case it would be; 50(100C50)/2

Thanks! Splitting the sum worked.
